WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
The Gospels were written by
believers, decades after Jesus died.

2
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.520
So historians ask a hard question.

3
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.680
Which words and deeds really go
back to the man from Nazareth?

4
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.390
Two famous scholars, John
Dominic Crossan and Tom Wright,

5
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.050
took up the challenge.

6
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.140
One finds a peasant rebel.

7
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.480
The other finds the Messiah.

8
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:26.820
How can two experts study the same
Jesus and reach such different answers?

9
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:31.270
In this mission, you'll meet Crossan's
social revolutionary and Wright's true

10
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.430
Messiah.

11
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.850
Then you'll weigh up how far each
scholar's approach can be trusted.

12
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.780
Your mission: explain how two careful
historians reach such different pictures

13
00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:42.680
of Jesus.
